appId: org.commcare.dalvik
tags:
  - install
  - partial
---
# Master Mobile Plan (2026) > Install > "Install 1" - Scan Barcode Install.
# Previously marked Not automatable: steps 4-6 require scanning a QR
# barcode rendered on a live HQ desktop-browser page with the device's own
# camera - a cross-surface (webpage <-> device camera) interaction
# BrowserStack's Maestro sessions have no camera-image-injection hook for
# (confirmed dead end this session for the identical class of interaction -
# Mobile Pins' own "Claim Privileges" QR-claim step).
#
# The row's REAL intent - publish the most recent build with multimedia
# included, install it via the code HQ's own barcode encodes, land on the
# login screen - is fully testable another way: the barcode is just a
# visual encoding of the SAME short alphanumeric code HQ's "Enter app code
# on installation screen" panel shows right next to it on that same
# Releases-page dialog (confirmed via HQClient.get_app_install_code's own
# docstring/citation - both are generated from the identical
# odk/<build_id>/short_odk_media_url endpoint). scripts/hq_client.py's
# resolve_app_codes() already resolves APP_CODE_BASIC_TESTS this exact way
# (get_app_install_code(app_id, include_media=True) - True is the default,
# matching this row's own "Include Multimedia" checkbox) before every run,
# and flows/common/install_app_by_code.yaml already drives the resulting
# "Enter Code" install path start-to-finish (see that file's own extensive
# citations), landing on edit_username - the exact outcome this row's own
# step 8 describes ("verify you are brought to the login page").
#
# What stays untested: the literal camera-pointed-at-a-screen gesture
# itself (steps 4-6). Everything downstream of that gesture - the publish/
# include-media/install/reach-login-page outcome the row actually cares
# about - is real, verified coverage, not a stand-in.
- runFlow:
    file: ../common/install_app_by_code.yaml
    env:
      APP_CODE: ${APP_CODE_BASIC_TESTS}
- assertVisible:
    id: "org.commcare.dalvik:id/edit_username"
